DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       These functions return the result  of  multiplying  the  floating‐point
       number _x by 2 raised to the power _e.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, these functions return _x _* _(_2_^_e_).

       If _e is zero, then _x is returned.

       If _x is a NaN, a NaN is returned.

       If _x is positive infinity (negative infinity), positive infinity (nega‐
       tive infinity) is returned.

       If the result underflows, a range error occurs, and zero is returned.

       If the result overflows, a range error occurs, and the functions return
       HHUUGGEE__VVAALL,  HHUUGGEE__VVAALLFF,  or HHUUGGEE__VVAALLLL, respectively, with a sign the same
       as _x.

